 After reflecting on-- Splitting up the half-angle.. Let us square both sides to recover a useful identity:  \begin{align*} \sin^2 \frac{\theta}{2} &= \left(\sqrt{\frac{x-1}{2x}} \right)^2 \\ &\Rightarrow \frac{1 - \cos \theta}{2} &= \frac{x-1}{2x} \\ &\Rightarrow \cos \theta = 1 - \frac{x-1}{x} \\ &\Rightarrow \cos \theta = \frac{2}{x}. \end{align*}

Then based on the half-angle identity from above, we have \begin{align*}\tan \theta &= \frac{2\sin \frac{\theta}{2}}{1-\cos \theta} \\ &= \frac{2 \cdot \sqrt{\frac{x-1}{2x}}}{1 - \frac{2}{x}} \\ &= \frac{2 \cdot \sqrt{\frac{x-1}{2x}}}{\frac{x-2}{x}} \\ &= \frac{2x \cdot \sqrt{\frac{x-1}{2x}}}{x-2} = \frac{2\sqrt{2x^2-x^2+2x}}{x-2} \\ &= \frac{2x\sqrt{2x-1}}{x-2}.\end{align*}
有两种可能性：$x \ge 2$ 和 $x < 2$. 我们(swaps the fractions of two lines above. Namely, if $x \ge 2$, we have \begin{align*}\tan \theta &= \frac{2 \cdot \sqrt{\frac{x-1}{2x}}}{1 - \frac{2}{x}} \\ &= \frac{2 \cdot \sqrt{\frac{x-1}{2x}}}{\frac{x-2}{x}} \\ &=\frac{2x \cdot \sqrt{\frac{x-1}{2x}}}{x-2} = \frac{2\sqrt{2x^2-x^2+2x}}{x-2} \\ &= \frac{2x\sqrt{2x-1}}{x-2}.\end{align*}

if $x < 2$, we have \begin{align*}\tan \theta &= \frac{2 \cdot \sqrt{\frac{2x-1}{x}}}{1 - -\frac{2}{x}} \\ &= \frac{2 \cdot \sqrt{\frac{2x-1}{x}}}{\frac{x+2}{x}} \\ &= \frac{2x \cdot \sqrt{\frac{2x-1}{x}}}{x+2} = \frac{2\sqrt{2x^2-x^2+2x}}{x+2} \\ &= \frac{-2x\sqrt{2x-1}}{2-x}.\end{align*}所以 <answer> Suppose that $x \ge 2$. Then $\sqrt{x^2}=x,$ so the answer posted before is $\tan \theta = \boxed{\frac{2x\sqrt{2x-1}}{x-2}}$. On the other hand, if $x < 2$, the answer is $\boxed{\frac{-2x\sqrt{2x-1}}{x-2}}.

